    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Question\n\nIs there a way to configure a Python multiline string with `mini.ai`? I tried using `gen_spec.pair` but it does not accept multiple characters when using the `balanced` type.\r\n\r\nAnother non-solution is using the treesitter group `@string.documentation` as this only applies to docstrings, not multiline strings generally. For example:\r\n```python\r\nx = \"\"\"hello\r\nworld\"\"\"\r\n```\r\nThis is not a docstring, so a treesitter text object for that group does not help.\r\n\r\nI also tried creating composed patterns but could not get them to be balanced.",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.ai</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Is there a way to configure a Python multiline string with <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.ai</code>? I tried using <code class=\"notranslate\">gen_spec.pair</code> but it does not accept multiple characters when using the <code class=\"notranslate\">balanced</code> type.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Another non-solution is using the treesitter group <code class=\"notranslate\">@string.documentation</code> as this only applies to docstrings, not multiline strings generally. For example:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-python notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"x = &quot;&quot;&quot;hello\nworld&quot;&quot;&quot;\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-s1\">x</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\">\"\"\"hello</span>\n<span class=\"pl-s\">world\"\"\"</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is not a docstring, so a treesitter text object for that group does not help.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I also tried creating composed patterns but could not get them to be balanced.</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.ai\nQuestion\nIs there a way to configure a Python multiline string with mini.ai? I tried using gen_spec.pair but it does not accept multiple characters when using the balanced type.\nAnother non-solution is using the treesitter group @string.documentation as this only applies to docstrings, not multiline strings generally. For example:\nx = \"\"\"hello\nworld\"\"\"\nThis is not a docstring, so a treesitter text object for that group does not help.\nI also tried creating composed patterns but could not get them to be balanced.",
    "category": {
        "createdAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z",
        "description": "Ask the community for help",
        "emoji": ":pray:",
        "emojiHTML": "<div>🙏</div>",
        "id": "DIC_kwDOFoksYM4CAgqN",
        "isAnswerable": true,
        "name": "Q&A",
        "slug": "q-a",
        "updatedAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z"
    },
    "closed": true,
    "closedAt": "2025-10-30T09:21:36Z",
    "comment_count": 1,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Yes, this is possible with the following setup:\r\n\r\n- Create a '~/.config/nvim/after/ftplugin/python.lua' file with the following content:\r\n\r\n    ```lua\r\n    vim.b.miniai_config = {\r\n      custom_textobjects = {\r\n        -- Match triple \" or ' pair, `i` textobject is inside of them\r\n        s = { { '\"\"\".-\"\"\"', \"'''.-'''\" }, '^...().*()...$' },\r\n      },\r\n    }\r\n    ```\r\n- Use it like `is` and `as`. This will only work for Python files (i.e. in buffers with `python` filetype).",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Yes, this is possible with the following setup:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Create a '~/.config/nvim/after/ftplugin/python.lua' file with the following content:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"vim.b.miniai_config = {\n  custom_textobjects = {\n    -- Match triple &quot; or ' pair, `i` textobject is inside of them\n    s = { { '&quot;&quot;&quot;.-&quot;&quot;&quot;', &quot;'''.-'''&quot; }, '^...().*()...$' },\n  },\n}\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">b</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">miniai_config</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">custom_textobjects</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n    <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> Match triple \" or ' pair, `i` textobject is inside of them</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">s</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { { <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>\"\"\".-\"\"\"<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>'''.-'''<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span>}, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>^...().*()...$<span class=\"pl-pds\">' </span></span>},\n  },\n}</pre></div>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Use it like <code class=\"notranslate\">is</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">as</code>. This will only work for Python files (i.e. in buffers with <code class=\"notranslate\">python</code> filetype).</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
            "bodyText": "Yes, this is possible with the following setup:\n\n\nCreate a '~/.config/nvim/after/ftplugin/python.lua' file with the following content:\nvim.b.miniai_config = {\n  custom_textobjects = {\n    -- Match triple \" or ' pair, `i` textobject is inside of them\n    s = { { '\"\"\".-\"\"\"', \"'''.-'''\" }, '^...().*()...$' },\n  },\n}\n\n\nUse it like is and as. This will only work for Python files (i.e. in buffers with python filetype).",
