                    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
                    "body": "This doesn't seem to be balanced. For example:\r\n```\r\n\"\"\"hello\"\"\" x \"\"\"world\"\"\"\r\n```\r\nIf you use `vis` when the cursor is at `x`, it selects the `x` with the surrounding whitespace. But this shouldn't be valid since the strings in this case are `hello` and `world`.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">This doesn't seem to be balanced. For example:</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"&quot;&quot;&quot;hello&quot;&quot;&quot; x &quot;&quot;&quot;world&quot;&quot;&quot;\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">\"\"\"hello\"\"\" x \"\"\"world\"\"\"\n</code></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">If you use <code class=\"notranslate\">vis</code> when the cursor is at <code class=\"notranslate\">x</code>, it selects the <code class=\"notranslate\">x</code> with the surrounding whitespace. But this shouldn't be valid since the strings in this case are <code class=\"notranslate\">hello</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">world</code>.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "This doesn't seem to be balanced. For example:\n\"\"\"hello\"\"\" x \"\"\"world\"\"\"\n\nIf you use vis when the cursor is at x, it selects the x with the surrounding whitespace. But this shouldn't be valid since the strings in this case are hello and world.",
